.TH AUDIOSCOUT 1 "October 22, 2026" "audioscout 1.0.0" "AudioScout"
.SH NAME
audioscout \- fast audio catalog listening and editing tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audioscout
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AudioScout scans a directory tree for audio files (WAV, FLAC, MP3, OGG, AIFF,
CAF) and presents them in a sortable table with waveform or spectrogram
previews. It supports playback via bundled or external players, time markers,
selection-based editing (mute, normalize, delete), undo/redo, and persistent
session and column settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I directory
Optional path to the audio directory to open at startup. If omitted, the last
directory used in the previous session is restored from
.B ~/.config/AudioScout/config.json
and the SQLite database under
.BR ~/.local/share/AudioScout/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/AudioScout/config.json
Application settings: hotkeys, preview modes, column order, visibility and widths.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/AudioScout/audioscout.db
SQLite database with markers, preview cache metadata and session state.
.TP
.B ~/.cache/AudioScout/previews/
Generated PNG waveform/spectrogram previews.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at <https://github.com/alex-kurochkin/audioscan/issues>.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the AudioScout project.
